Well, you can...  But see, I wrote this while still in shock and hoping 
for a therapeutic effect of the writing (which will be stronger if it is 
longer).  Two valks in a row killed by suicide!  And what's more, 
unintentional suicide :-(.

The last one seems explicable only by the fact that it has been quite a 
number of years since I saw the valkyrie quest the last time.  My notion 
of it being easy (which I still believe) referred to its quest nemesis 
mostly.  There are some pitfalls in that quest, of course.  Levitation 
or flying are essential, otherwise you might even be drowned by a fire 
trap in the ice.  This I took into accout, the drawbridge I did not. 
Maybe I should not play the game without colors anymore (but I do not 
know how to teach it to recognize that my linux machine does indeed have 
colored xterms or dtterms...).  The first valk would definitely not have 
stepped in the lava pool had it been red, the second might have checked 
what is ahead, had she seen that the ground changed color to brown on 
the drawbridge.

It seems that the valk quest is the only one in vanilla (I have no way 
of knowing the additional slashem quests) that has a drawbridge in the 
final level...

